t The Rotunda shopping center in Baltimore, and the transmitter is based atop Television Hill in the city\'s Woodberry district.', 'WZFG | WZFG (1100 AM, "The Flag") is a 50,000 watt radio station serving the Fargo-Moorhead market, licensed to Dilworth, Minnesota. Its two-tower transmitter site is near Sabin, Minnesota. The station is owned by Bakken Beacon Media.', 'WLPZ-LP | WLPZ-LP (95.1 FM) is a community radio station licensed to Leominster, Massachusetts and serves the Leominster area. Its broadcast license is held by the City of Leominster.', "WLGZ-FM | WLGZ-FM (102.7 FM) is a radio station broadcasting an oldies/classic hits format. The station is licensed to Webster, New York, serving the Rochester, New York area, and is currently owned by DJRO Broadcasting LLC. Studios are in Rochester's east side, while the transmitter tower is in the city's west side."]
