ason of "Mad Men" in 2007, writing the episode "The Hobo Code" and co-writing the episode "Shoot." Alongside his colleagues on the writing staff he won a WGA award for best new series; he was also nominated for the award for best dramatic series and best episodic drama for "The Hobo Code." He served as an executive story editor on the first season of "Justified" in 2010, writing "Long in the Tooth" and co-writing "The Hammer."']
